// CodeContinue - Key Bindings
// 
// DEFAULT KEYBINDING: Not implemented by default to prevent conflicts.
// You have to set it up once.
// 
// HOW TO SET UP (SPLIT VIEW):
// 1. Go to: Preferences > Package Settings > CodeContinue > Key Bindings
//    (or press Ctrl+Shift+P >> "Preferences: CodeContinue Key Bindings")
// 2. COPY the desired keybinding setting from the LEFT pane (this file).
// 3. PASTE it into the RIGHT pane (User keymap) inside the [ ... ] list.
// 4. SAVE the User keymap file (Ctrl+S / Cmd+S).
// 
// Example configurations to copy to the right pane:
//
// Option 1: Ctrl+Enter (Recommended, no conflicts)
// { "keys": ["ctrl+enter"], "command": "code_continue_accept" }
//
// Option 2: Tab key (only triggers when suggestion phantom is visible)
// {
//     "keys": ["tab"],
//     "command": "code_continue_accept",
//     "context": [
//         { "key": "code_continue_visible", "operator": "equal", "operand": true }
//     ]
// }
//
// Option 3: Right Arrow key
// { "keys": ["right"], "command": "code_continue_accept" }
//
// Option 4: End key
// { "keys": ["end"], "command": "code_continue_accept" }

